ANGLE 7: is L(S) = sum_Lambda prod h  a tournament partition function H=I(Omega,2)?
==============================================================================

--- (C) THE TWO SEVENS ---
 tournament side: Phi_3(2) = 2^2+2+1 = 7  (forbidden phantom; orbit 7*3^k)
 forbidden H orbit: [7, 21, 63, 189]
 LRC side: band denom n=14=2*7; kernel s(t)=sin(pi t/7)/(pi t); s(t)=0 iff 7|t
 check s(t)=0 exactly at multiples of 7 (cyclotomic vanishing of the kernel):
     s( 0) = +0.142857
     s( 1) = +0.138109
     s( 6) = +0.023018
     s( 7) = +0.000000  <-- ZERO (7|t)
     s( 8) = -0.017264
     s(13) = -0.010624
     s(14) = -0.000000  <-- ZERO (7|t)
     s(21) = +0.000000  <-- ZERO (7|t)
 NOTE: the LRC 7 is the DENOMINATOR n/2 = 14/2 = 7 of the danger band 1/14.
       The tournament 7 = Phi_3(2), the cyclotomic value of x^2+x+1 at the
       OCF fugacity x=2. These are 7 from DIFFERENT mechanisms:
         LRC 7   = half the runner count (geometry of the circle / band size)
         OCF 7   = Phi_3(2) (algebra: 3-cycle generating fn at fugacity 2)
       Same NUMBER, different generators. -> shallow unless a map identifies them.

  Probe: does any natural fugacity z give Phi_3(z) = 7 or 14?
     Phi_3(1) = 3;  Phi_2(1)=z+1=2;  Phi_6(1)=z*z-z+1=1
     Phi_3(2) = 7;  Phi_2(2)=z+1=3;  Phi_6(2)=z*z-z+1=3
     Phi_3(3) = 13;  Phi_2(3)=z+1=4;  Phi_6(3)=z*z-z+1=7
     Phi_3(4) = 21;  Phi_2(4)=z+1=5;  Phi_6(4)=z*z-z+1=13
     Phi_3(5) = 31;  Phi_2(5)=z+1=6;  Phi_6(5)=z*z-z+1=21
  -> Phi_3(2)=7 (z=2) and Phi_6(... ) etc. The OCF 7 needs z=2 EXACTLY.
     The LRC 7 is independent of any fugacity. Coincidence of the integer 7.

--- (A)+(B) SIDE-BY-SIDE on the extremizer core S={1..13}\{6} U {98} ---
 S = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 98]  |S| = 13
